    "content": "No Kings Day is a series of massive, nationwide, and largely peaceful protest rallies in the U.S. designed to oppose perceived authoritarianism and policies of the Trump administration. The movement, which draws millions across all 50 states, emphasizes that the country belongs to its people rather than kings. Usage Examples & Context Mass Mobilization: Nationwide rallies featuring protests in over 2,700 cities, such as those held in October 2025 and March 2026, often targeting federal immigration enforcement (ICE), the cost of living, and executive actions. Digital Organizing: The movement uses digital platforms to organize rallies in both major cities and smaller towns, emphasizing grassroots, nonviolent action. Resistance Symbolism: Participants use the events to defend democratic norms, often waving American flags and chanting against the administration. Synonyms and Related Terms No Kings Day of Action No Kings Day of Peaceful Action No Kings rallies Anti-Trump protests Day of defiance No Kings movement Organizers and participants include a broad coalition of activists, union members (such as AFSCME), and concerned citizens aiming to strengthen democracy and defend civil liberties.",
